# Pipeline Endpoint Required Query Params Contract

When an API route in the pipeline endpoint matrix requires one or more query
parameters for a valid request, the concrete pipeline endpoint spec must include
those parameters.

## Trigger conditions

- Any change to endpoint behavior that makes a previously optional query
  parameter required.
- Any change to parameter validation/error handling for endpoints included in:
  - `hpcperfstats/tests/urlconf_route_catalog.py`
  - `tests/pipeline_e2e/test_all_endpoints_browser.py`
  - `hpcperfstats/tests/test_endpoint_route_snapshot.py`
- Any route contract update under Django URL/API files that affects status-band
  expectations in the pipeline endpoint smoke tests.

## Required actions

- Update `build_pipeline_http_endpoint_specs(...)` so each affected route uses a
  valid parameterized `path` (for example include `?group=...` when required).
- Keep `PipelineHttpEndpointSpec.route_template` unchanged for template
  coverage; only adjust concrete `path` and status/content expectations.
- Update endpoint-specific assertions in
  `tests/pipeline_e2e/test_all_endpoints_browser.py` to support parameterized
  paths (for example use prefix matching rather than strict equality when
  asserting a route family).
- Re-run:
  - `hpcperfstats/tests/test_endpoint_route_snapshot.py`
  - `tests/pipeline_e2e/test_all_endpoints_browser.py` (compose workflow)

## Why

- The pipeline browser/API matrix should assert real, contract-valid requests.
- Bare route probes that omit required query parameters create false failures and
  hide genuine regressions.

## Overlap

- Complements `pipeline-endpoint-matrix-drift-guard.mdc`.
- Complements `web-pages-e2e-test-maintenance.mdc` for browser-E2E expectations.
